 "response": "Tido's budget is now **$3,930K**.\n\n**Method**\n- **Which records count:** Only Finance Office updates change the budget. PMO, Vendor, Legal, Sales, Engineering, Marketing, Operations and Facilities messages are ignored. Finance notes that don't change the budget (audits, receipts, cost-center codes) are also ignored.\n- **Resolving withdrawals:** I traced each chain of withdrawals to its last link. A withdrawal counts only if nothing later withdraws it.\n  - Example: #0575 withdraws #0175, so #0175 has no effect. That means #0031 stands, #0031 cancels #0011, and #0007 (+$303K) is restored.\n  - Similar chains restore #0008, #0010, #0040, #0041, #0132, #0166, #0131, #0098, #0191, #0006, #0261, #0181's withdrawal-of-withdrawal (#0402) and others.\n  - Other chains remove updates for good. Examples: #0002, #0004, #0028, #0083, #0088, #0117, #0248, #0059, #0299, #0344, #0427, #0430 and #0443.\n- **Calculation:** Starting from #0001 ($1,650K), I applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in order.\n\nI did this in a single pass and did not run a separate second calculation. While working through the list I caught and corrected a few missed withdrawals (#0432, #0587 and #1019), so a small error elsewhere in this long list is possible.\n\nANSWER: $3930K",
